   "in_scope": true,
   "out_of_scope_reason": null,
   "unmapped": [
    "Privacy is shuffle-model (eps,delta)-DP: each batch of users' rewards is aggregated via an (eps,delta)-SDP shuffle mechanism; the learner knows the privacy parameter delta_dp as well as eps_dp",
    "Batch sizes are chosen adaptively by the server on the fly (not a fixed predetermined number of batches); the server only observes privatized batch sums",
    "Each user participates in exactly one batch with a single round of communication"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "The \\textit{shuffle-model MAB} setting involves repeating the following process until the $T$'th player pulls its arm: The server selects a batch size $m$, a \\textit{batch} of $m$ random fresh new users, and an $m$-user single-round SDP mechanism $M$. It then picks an arm $a\\in [k]$ that all $m$ users of the batch pull. ... Each user $i$ determines binary reward from pulling the arm $a$. ... The server computes $M(\\{r_i\\}_{i\\in batch})$ using the rewards $r_i$."
  }
 ],
